// Conceptually: clone a node fresh every time it is encountered during
// traversal, without any tracking of already-cloned nodes. This creates
// duplicate clone objects for the same original node, and causes
// INFINITE recursion whenever the graph contains a cycle (which is
// common, since the graph is undirected and connected, not necessarily
// a tree).

